From: Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>
Subject: Support uuid-utils >= 1.0 uuid7(nanoseconds=...) signature

uuid-utils 1.0 intentionally changed uuid7/uuid6/uuid8 to the
signatures Python 3.14 added to the standard library and removed the
legacy 0.x keywords (timestamp=, nanos=). langsmith calls
uuid_utils.compat.uuid7(timestamp=seconds, nanos=nanos), which raises
TypeError: uuid7() got an unexpected keyword argument 'timestamp' and
fails 159 unit tests in %check.

Try the 1.0 nanoseconds= keyword first, fall back to the 0.x
timestamp=/nanos= pair so the same code works with both.

--- langsmith-0.14.17.orig/src/langsmith/_internal/_uuid.py
+++ langsmith-0.14.17/src/langsmith/_internal/_uuid.py
@@ -42,8 +42,11 @@
     # For now, just delegate to the uuid_utils implementation
     if nanoseconds is None:
         return _uuid_utils_uuid7()
-    seconds, nanos = _to_timestamp_and_nanos(nanoseconds)
-    return _uuid_utils_uuid7(timestamp=seconds, nanos=nanos)
+    try:
+        return _uuid_utils_uuid7(nanoseconds=nanoseconds)
+    except TypeError:
+        seconds, nanos = _to_timestamp_and_nanos(nanoseconds)
+        return _uuid_utils_uuid7(timestamp=seconds, nanos=nanos)
 
 
 def is_uuid_v7(uuid_obj: uuid.UUID) -> bool:
